@startuml
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram: UC3 Process Rental, payment and completion (Contract 4 for a rental), W11 draft
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc3_pay_rental.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc3_pay_rental.puml
' Participants: classes of the logical view (architecture.md 4.2) and of the design class diagram skeleton. Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.4, 4.1 to 4.3; PaymentMethod of AD-08.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 115
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #444444
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F4F8FD
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam SequenceReferenceBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8A04A
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam LegendBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 190

title NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram: UC3 Process Rental, payment and completion (Contract 4)

box "UI layer (ui.api)" #F4F8FD
  participant ":Rental\nController" as Ctl
end box
box "Application / domain layer" #F4F8FD
  participant ":Rental\nHandler" as H
  participant ":Payment\nMethods" as PMs
  participant "pm:\nPaymentMethod" as PM
  participant "rental:\nRental" as R
end box
box "application.interfaces" #F4F8FD
  participant ":CashDrawer" as Dr
  participant ":CardReader" as CR
  participant ":PaymentService" as Pay
  participant ":Transaction\nRepository" as Repo
  participant ":Receipt\nPrinter" as Pr
end box

== makePayment(amount, tenderType) - Contract 4, for a rental (UC3 steps 13-16) ==
[-> Ctl : POST /api/rentals/{rentalID}/payment {"amount", "tenderType"}
Ctl -> H : makePayment(amount, tenderType)
H -> R : canBePaid(amount, tenderType)
note right of R
  Rental ended, no payment yet (one tender per
  rental, BR-18). The total includes the deposit;
  a card deposit is charged and refunded (SRS 5.3 Q2).
end note
R --> H : OK (else 409 / 422)
H -> PMs : get(tenderType)
PMs --> H : pm
H -> PM : pay(rental, amount)
note right of PM
  Polymorphism (AD-08): the handler never checks the tender.
  CashPaymentMethod, CreditCardPaymentMethod or CheckPaymentMethod.
  Each one creates its own Payment subclass (Creator).
  The same PaymentMethods as in UC1 (dsd_uc1_makePayment).
end note

alt cash (13a): CashPaymentMethod
  PM -> PM : amount >= total? (BR-06)
  alt amount lower than the total
    PM --> H : REJECTED
  else
    PM -> Dr : open(CASH_PAYMENT, employeeID)
    Dr --> PM : OPENED or ERROR (logged, IR-14)
    PM -> PM : create CashPayment(amount, change due)
    PM -> R : setPayment(p)
    PM --> H : APPROVED
  end
else credit card (13b): CreditCardPaymentMethod
  PM -> CR : read()
  CR --> PM : CardReadResult
  alt ERROR (13b1a)
    PM --> H : READ_ERROR
  else OK, cardToken
    PM -> Pay : authorize(PaymentRequest(rental.transactionID, total, cardToken))
    note right of Pay
      The rental ID is the same in every retry (IR-02).
      The card token is never stored (IR-12, AD-09).
      Timeout 10 s in the adapter (AD-07).
    end note
    alt APPROVED
      Pay --> PM : PaymentResult(APPROVED, authCode, reference, last4)
      PM -> Repo : saveOpenAuthorization(rental.transactionID, reference)
      note right of Repo
        Voided at start-up if the register stops
        before saveCompleted (IR-15, AD-07).
      end note
      PM -> PM : create CreditCardPayment\n(amount, authCode, reference, last4)
      PM -> R : setPayment(p)
      PM --> H : APPROVED
    else DECLINED (13b2a)
      Pay --> PM : PaymentResult(DECLINED, reason)
      PM --> H : DECLINED
    else NOT_AVAILABLE (13b2b)
      Pay --> PM : PaymentResult(NOT_AVAILABLE)
      PM --> H : NOT_AVAILABLE
    end
  end
else check (13c, Could): CheckPaymentMethod
  PM -> Pay : authorize(PaymentRequest: CHECK)
  Pay --> PM : PaymentResult
  PM --> H : APPROVED (CheckPayment set as for a card) or DECLINED
end

alt APPROVED
  H -> R : setItemsRented() <<new>>
  note right of R
    item.status = Rented for each line (BR-11),
    as reduceStock() for a sale.
  end note
  H -> R : createAccountingRecord()
  R --> H : record (rental fee, tax, deposit shown apart,\ntaxToBeCorrected; BR-14)
  H -> Repo : saveCompleted(rental, record)
  note right of Repo
    ONE database transaction (AD-05, AD-06): the rental with its lines,
    payment, new customer (if any) and item status Rented, the AccountingQueue
    record, the entry of store_sync_list, and the open authorization is deleted.
    In the store database the same transaction sets Rented and removes the hold.
    The Accounting System gets the record later (AccountingSender, IR-06, 15a).
  end note
  H -> R : getReceipt()
  R --> H : rental receipt (FR-39: item and serial number,\nfee, tax, deposit, total, due date,\ncustomer ID as text and barcode)
  H -> Pr : print(receipt)
  Pr --> H : READY (NO_PAPER or ERROR: the rental is saved,\nreprint later, 16a)
  H --> Ctl : APPROVED, receiptNumber, change due or last4 and authCode
  [<-- Ctl : 200 result APPROVED; rental receipt (S-06)
else REJECTED, READ_ERROR or DECLINED
  note over H, R
    No Payment is created and the rental stays open: the Cashier reads the card again
    or chooses another tender (BR-18, FR-66, FR-67).
  end note
  H --> Ctl : result and reason
  [<-- Ctl : 200 result REJECTED, READ_ERROR or DECLINED, reason
else NOT_AVAILABLE (13b2b)
  H --> Ctl : NOT_AVAILABLE (retry allowed)
  [<-- Ctl : 200 result NOT_AVAILABLE: retry, another tender or cancel
  ref over Ctl, Pay
    The rental stays open (IR-02, FR-66). Retry: the same makePayment with the same rental ID; the card is read
    again (AD-09). Other tender or cancelRental: first pm.giveUp(rental), which sends voidAuthorization with the
    same rental ID (IR-15, AD-07). The same as for a sale (dsd_uc1_makePayment, ui_design.md 5.2).
  end ref
end

legend bottom left
  **GRASP**
  Controller: RentalController and RentalHandler, as in the other UC3 diagrams.
  Polymorphism, Protected Variations: the payment goes through PaymentMethod (AD-08); a new tender is a new class and no
  handler changes (NFR-09). PaymentMethods (Pure Fabrication) gives the PaymentMethod of each tender type.
  Creator: each PaymentMethod creates its own Payment subclass; Rental creates its AccountingRecord, because it has its data (as Sale in UC1).
  Information Expert: Rental knows whether it can be paid (BR-18), sets the status of its items and makes its receipt; CashPaymentMethod checks BR-06.
  Low Coupling, Indirection: the handler sees only interfaces (PaymentService, CardReader, CashDrawer, TransactionRepository,
  ReceiptPrinter); the timeouts are in the adapters and the fallbacks in the handler (AD-07).
endlegend
@enduml
